#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:164
msgid "``rcl_logging_implementation``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:166
msgid ""
"A new ``rcl_logging_implementation`` package has been introduced to allow "
"users to select the logging backend implementation at runtime without "
"rebuilding ``rcl``. Users can set the ``RCL_LOGGING_IMPLEMENTATION`` "
"environment variable to switch between available logging backends (e.g., "
"``rcl_logging_spdlog``, ``rcl_logging_noop``, or custom implementations). If "
"not specified, ``rcl_logging_spdlog`` is used by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:170
msgid ""
"See https://github.com/ros2/rcl/issues/1178, https://github.com/ros2/rcl/"
"pull/1276, and https://github.com/ros2/rcl_logging/pull/135 for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:173
msgid "``rclcpp``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:175
msgid ""
"Added new `Callback Group Events Executor <https://github.com/ros2/rclcpp/"
"pull/3097>`__. Like its predecessor the experimental ``EventsExecutor``, the "
"``EventsCBGExecutor`` uses an events queue to process ready entities. Builds "
"on the experimental ``EventsExecutor`` by adding support for multiple "
"sources of ROS time and multiple threads. Compared to the Single and "
"Multithreaded Executors, the ``EventsCBGExecutor`` exhibits around 10 to 15% "
"less CPU usage. Note: The experimental ``EventsExecutor`` is now deprecated. "
"For similar performance, use the ``EventsCBGExecutor`` with one thread."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:185
msgid ""
"`Unified component container interface <https://github.com/ros2/rclcpp/"
"pull/3134>`__ - ``component_container`` is now the single entrypoint for "
"launching both regular and isolated component containers with all types of "
"executors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:189
msgid ""
"Added ``disable_callbacks()`` and ``enable_callbacks()`` APIs to "
"``SubscriptionBase``. By design the subscription itself is a shared pointer "
"and its callbacks are propagated to the executor, making it difficult to "
"manage subscription lifecycle from the application side. When a subscription "
"is deleted at the application layer, it may still be referenced by the node "
"and executor, causing callbacks to be invoked unexpectedly. This can lead to "
"undefined behavior when the callback accesses resources that have been "
"cleaned up. The new APIs allow users to disable subscription callbacks at "
"runtime without destroying the subscription, preventing unexpected callback "
"invocations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:200
msgid ""
"See `ros2/rclcpp#2984 <https://github.com/ros2/rclcpp/issues/2984>`__ and "
"`ros2/rclcpp#2985 <https://github.com/ros2/rclcpp/pull/2985>`__ for more "
"details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:204
msgid "``rclpy``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:207
msgid "Native asyncio support with ``AsyncNode`` (experimental)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:209
msgid ""
"Added ``AsyncNode``, a new node type that runs on the ``asyncio`` event "
"loop. Subscription, service, and timer callbacks can now ``await`` any "
"asyncio operation. The new async ``client.call(request)`` and sim-time aware "
"``clock.sleep(...)`` are awaitable from any asyncio task. CPU usage is "
"significantly reduced compared to the ``SingleThreadedExecutor``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:214
msgid ""
"See the `Writing an async node with asyncio <../../lyrical/Tutorials/"
"Intermediate/Writing-An-Async-Node-With-Asyncio-Python.html>`__ tutorial and "
"https://github.com/ros2/rclpy/pull/1620 for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:217
msgid "``rosbag2``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:219
msgid ""
"``Rosbag2`` received several new recording, playback, observability, and API "
"improvements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:221
msgid ""
"Added support for repeating transient-local messages when recording bags. "
"Users can configure selected transient-local topics with ``--repeat-"
"transient-local`` and an optional per-topic depth, or use ``--repeat-all-"
"transient-local`` to automatically apply the behavior to topics whose "
"publishers offer ``TRANSIENT_LOCAL`` durability QoS. This helps preserve "
"latched/static state, such as maps or static transforms, across bag splits "
"and snapshots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:228
msgid ""
"See `ros2/rosbag2#2385 <https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/pull/2385>`__, `ros2/"
"rosbag2#2386 <https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/pull/2386>`__, `ros2/"
"rosbag2#2387 <https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/pull/2387>`__, and `ros2/"
"rosbag2#2391 <https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/pull/2391>`__ for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:233
msgid ""
"Added recorder service APIs for starting and stopping recording, starting "
"and stopping topic discovery, and querying whether discovery is running. "
"This makes it possible to control a recorder process remotely through ROS "
"services instead of only through the command-line process lifecycle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:238
msgid ""
"See `ros2/rosbag2#2248 <https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/pull/2248>`__ for "
"more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:240
msgid ""
"Added scheduled service operations for coordinated recording and playback "
"workflows. Record, play, resume, and split operations can now be scheduled "
"by time, with support for node time, publish time, and receive time modes "
"where applicable. Service responses were also extended with explicit return "
"codes and error strings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:245
msgid ""
"See `ros2/rosbag2#2330 <https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/pull/2330>`__ and "
"`ros2/rosbag2#2357 <https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/pull/2357>`__ for more "
"details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:248
msgid ""
"Added circular logging by split count. When recording with bag splitting "
"enabled, ``--max-bag-files`` limits the maximum number of bag files stored "
"on disk by automatically deleting the oldest split files as new ones are "
"created."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:253
msgid ""
"See `ros2/rosbag2#2218 <https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/pull/2218>`__ for "
"more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:255
msgid ""
"Added a time-bounded snapshot cache option, ``--max-cache-duration``. This "
"allows snapshot-mode recording to bound the cached data by duration in "
"addition to existing cache controls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:259
msgid ""
"See `ros2/rosbag2#2289 <https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/pull/2289>`__ for "
"more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:261
msgid ""
"Added message-loss observability during recording. ``Rosbag2`` can now "
"collect message-loss statistics from the transport layer and recorder "
"internals, and publish incremental per-topic loss events on the predefined "
"``events/rosbag2_messages_lost`` topic. The publishing rate can be "
"configured with ``--stats_max_publishing_rate``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:267
msgid ""
"See `ros2/rosbag2#2039 <https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/pull/2039>`__, `ros2/"
"rosbag2#2144 <https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/pull/2144>`__, and `ros2/"
"rosbag2#2150 <https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/pull/2150>`__ for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:271
msgid ""
"Expanded the ``rosbag2_py`` player and recorder APIs. Python users can now "
"programmatically control playback and recording with APIs such as pause, "
"resume, stop, seek, play-next, spin control, and wait helpers, instead of "
"relying only on blocking command-line-style helpers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:276
msgid ""
"See `ros2/rosbag2#2047 <https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/pull/2047>`__ and "
"`ros2/rosbag2#2062 <https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/pull/2062>`__ for more "
"details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:279
msgid ""
"Added APIs for querying player timing metadata. Users can now query the "
"player's starting time and playback duration, and Python readers can access "
"the send timestamp when reading serialized messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:283
msgid ""
"See `ros2/rosbag2#2061 <https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/pull/2061>`__ and "
"`ros2/rosbag2#2095 <https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/pull/2095>`__ for more "
"details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Releases/Release-Lyrical-Luth.rst:286
msgid ""
"Improved message definition resolution for recorded data. ``Rosbag2`` can "
